{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.TopologicalMassFormulaAlgebraic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.TopologicalMassFormulaAlgebraic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassFormula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassFormula","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula-algebraic.lean#L41-L65","doc":"**Algebraic topological mass formula.**\n\nGiven the algebraic-side data, the mass identity\n  mass_alg = phi1 · ℏ_q⁻²\nis an equality in the coefficient ring, with the invertibility\nof `hbar_sq` carried explicitly as a **unit** `u : Rˣ` with\n`↑u = hbar_sq` (§7c: the `Units` form over `[CommRing R]`\nrather than `x ≠ 0` over a field — the ring the narrative names,\n`ℤ[q^{±1/2}]` localised at `ℏ_q`, is not a field).  Taking\n`R` a field and `u = Units.mk0 hbar_sq h` recovers the divided\nform `mass_alg = phi1 / hbar_sq`.  The Archimedean version\n`prop:topological-mass-formula` is the specialisation under\n`τ_arch` at `q = q₀`.\n\nScope (2026-11-16): the mass formula enters as the hypothesis\n`h_phi1 : phi1 = mass_alg · ℏ_q²`; the theorem only multiplies by the\ninverse unit. It does not derive the formula, and none of the four\n`AlgebraicMassData` fields is tied to a braid. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:topological-mass-formula-algebraic","label":"prop:topological-mass-formula-algebraic","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula-algebraic.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassData.mass_alg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassData.mass_alg","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula-algebraic.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassData.phi1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassData.phi1","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula-algebraic.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassData.hbar_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassData.hbar_sq","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula-algebraic.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassData.vol_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassData.vol_q","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula-algebraic.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula-algebraic.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.AlgebraicMassData","kind":"structure","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/topological-mass-formula-algebraic.lean#L27-L39","doc":"Abstract data for the algebraic mass formula at a single\nclosed braid.\n\n`R` is the coefficient ring (instantiated as `ℤ[q^{±1/2}]` /\n`ℚ(q)` in the QOU narrative). `vol_q` is the algebraic\nquantum volume of the braid; `hbar_sq` is `ℏ_q²` in `R`;\n`phi1` is the Reeb / Archimedean specialisation\n`τ_arch(vol_q)`; `mass_alg` is the algebraic-side mass. ","signatureChunk":0}]}